* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
* Behavioral fully differential second-order SC biquad, Sky130-level-free
* prototype: ideal switches (ron = RON ohm), behavioral op-amps (finite DC
* gain A0, one-pole GBW, slew-rate clamp IMAXP), ideal non-overlapping clocks.
*
* Default configuration: K = 50, Q = 1, CI = 8 pF, fclk = 500 kHz,
* f0 = fclk/K = 10 kHz, step input.  The run scripts
* (sim/behavioral/run_sweep.py, sim/behavioral/extract_f0_q.py) rewrite the
* .param block below to sweep A0/GBW/SR/Ron or to set (K, Q); the stimulus
* line is rewritten to a sine tone for frequency-response extraction.
*
* Ideal-vs-real assumptions (also in docs/architecture.md):
*   - switches: linear ron, no charge injection, no clock feedthrough
*   - op-amp: fully differential, ideal CM, rails clamp at 0.05 V from supplies
*   - caps: exact values, no mismatch, no parasitic top-plate caps
*   - clocks: ideal 45% duty + 5% non-overlap gap, no jitter
*   - the double-plate sampling network implements bottom-plate early
*     sampling by construction (source plate releases before the summing
*     node connects).
*
* ngspice quirk: device values that are parameters MUST be braced, e.g.
* `C11 a b {CI}` -- an unbraced `C11 a b CI` silently gives a 0 F capacitor.

* --- parameter block (rewritten by the run scripts) ---
.param VCM=1.65
.param VDD=3.3
.param fclk=500000
.param T=1/fclk
.param CI=8p
.param Cs=1.171636p
.param Cd=1.265774p
.param Ron=1000
.param A0=1000
.param GBW=1e+07
.param SR=5e+06
.param VOS=0
.param CCOMP=1p
.param PIVAL=3.141592653589793
.param GMAMP=2*PIVAL*GBW*CCOMP
.param RAMP=A0/GMAMP
.param IMAXP=SR*CCOMP
.param DUTY=0.45
.param GUARD=0.05
.param AMP=0.05
.param TSTEP=100u

* ideal non-overlapping clocks (phi1 45% duty, 5% guard gap)
Vclk1 clk1 0 PULSE(0 3.3 0 1n 1n {DUTY*T} {T})
Vclk2 clk2 0 PULSE(0 3.3 {(DUTY+GUARD)*T} 1n 1n {DUTY*T} {T})
Vcm vcm 0 {VCM}

* step stimulus (default).  extract_f0_q.py rewrites this line to
* Vsig sig 0 SIN(0 {AMP} {FSIG})
Vsig sig 0 PWL(0 0 {TSTEP} 0 {TSTEP+1n} {AMP})
Bip vinp 0 V = VCM + V(sig)
Bin vinn 0 V = VCM - V(sig)

* ---- op-amp 1 (BP integrator) ----
Bd1 vd1 0 V = V(x1p)-V(x1n) + VOS
Bg1 0 n1 I = max(min(GMAMP*V(vd1), IMAXP), -IMAXP) - V(n1)/RAMP
Ccomp1 n1 0 {CCOMP}
Boutp1 bpp 0 V = max(min(VCM - 0.5*V(n1), VDD-0.05), 0.05)
Boutn1 bpn 0 V = max(min(VCM + 0.5*V(n1), VDD-0.05), 0.05)

* ---- op-amp 2 (LP integrator) ----
Bd2 vd2 0 V = V(x2p)-V(x2n) + VOS
Bg2 0 n2 I = max(min(GMAMP*V(vd2), IMAXP), -IMAXP) - V(n2)/RAMP
Ccomp2 n2 0 {CCOMP}
Boutp2 lpp 0 V = max(min(VCM - 0.5*V(n2), VDD-0.05), 0.05)
Boutn2 lpn 0 V = max(min(VCM + 0.5*V(n2), VDD-0.05), 0.05)

* common-mode hold on the virtual grounds (1 Gohm to VCM).
* The behavioral op-amp only senses the differential input, so without
* these the input CM is undetermined and the DC solve puts it at 0 V.
Rcm_x1p x1p vcm 1e9
Rcm_x1n x1n vcm 1e9
Rcm_x2p x2p vcm 1e9
Rcm_x2n x2n vcm 1e9

* integrator feedback caps
C11 x1p bpp {CI}
C12 x1n bpn {CI}
C21 x2p lpp {CI}
C22 x2n lpn {CI}

* Every input branch is a true double-plate sampling network:
*   phi1: cap charges between its source and VCM (op-amp side open)
*   phi2: source side goes to VCM, op-amp side connects to the
*         summing node -- the sampled charge is dumped into CI.
* Keeping the op-amp-side plate permanently attached (an earlier
* version) makes the net charge transfer per cycle exactly zero.

* Cs1: input -> BP integrator (straight)
C31 a1p s1p {Cs}
C32 a1n s1n {Cs}
S_a1p a1p x1p clk2 0 SW1
S_a1n a1n x1n clk2 0 SW1
S_b1p a1p vcm clk1 0 SW1
S_b1n a1n vcm clk1 0 SW1
S31 s1p vinp clk1 0 SW1
S32 s1n vinn clk1 0 SW1
S33 s1p vcm clk2 0 SW1
S34 s1n vcm clk2 0 SW1

* Cs2: BP -> LP, CROSS-coupled (p side samples bpn on phi1)
C41 a2p s2p {Cs}
C42 a2n s2n {Cs}
S_a2p a2p x2p clk2 0 SW1
S_a2n a2n x2n clk2 0 SW1
S_b2p a2p vcm clk1 0 SW1
S_b2n a2n vcm clk1 0 SW1
S41 s2p bpn clk1 0 SW1
S42 s2n bpp clk1 0 SW1
S43 s2p vcm clk2 0 SW1
S44 s2n vcm clk2 0 SW1

* Cs3: LP -> BP, straight (p side samples lpp on phi1)
C51 a3p s3p {Cs}
C52 a3n s3n {Cs}
S_a3p a3p x1p clk2 0 SW1
S_a3n a3n x1n clk2 0 SW1
S_b3p a3p vcm clk1 0 SW1
S_b3n a3n vcm clk1 0 SW1
S51 s3p lpp clk1 0 SW1
S52 s3n lpn clk1 0 SW1
S53 s3p vcm clk2 0 SW1
S54 s3n vcm clk2 0 SW1

* Cd: switched damping.  phi2: in parallel with CI1 (plates at
* x1 and BP output); phi1: both plates shorted to VCM.  During
* phi2 the charge stored on CI(CI+Cd)/(CI) splits CI:Cd, giving
* exactly the 1/(1+Cd/CI) factor of the discrete map.
C61 gd1p sd1p {Cd}
C62 gd1n sd1n {Cd}
S_gd1p gd1p x1p clk2 0 SW1
S_gd1n gd1n x1n clk2 0 SW1
S_hd1p gd1p vcm clk1 0 SW1
S_hd1n gd1n vcm clk1 0 SW1
S_wd1p sd1p bpp clk2 0 SW1
S_wd1n sd1n bpn clk2 0 SW1
S_xd1p sd1p vcm clk1 0 SW1
S_xd1n sd1n vcm clk1 0 SW1

.model SW1 SW vt=1.65 vh=0 ron={Ron} roff=1e12

.options reltol=1e-4 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-7 rshunt=1e15
.tran 1e-08 0.0015
.save v(lpp) v(lpn) v(bpp) v(bpn) v(vinp) v(vinn)
.control
run
set wr_singlescale
wrdata biquad_behav.dat v(lpp) v(lpn) v(bpp) v(bpn) v(vinp) v(vinn)
.endc
.end
